Z||000000||Zorba||12-02-2000||06:29 PM||||V-8<BR>My manifold leaked water into the engine. Caught early but how do I clean the mess inside the oil pan (and engine) (white milky sludge)? Is there a way to flush this out of the system? - <P>Performer manifold had a pucture hole in it that went undetected until after installation! Glad I caught this early in my garage instead of out on the road somewhere.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Archie||12-02-2000||10:24 PM||||I agree with what you were told on TechNet, buy some of that flush stuff and flush it out a couple of times. Don't forget to change the filter before & after Flushing.<P>Mario, While we are here.... with all the trouble you've had putting this thing together..... has it occured to you that maybe it would have been cheaper and maybe you would have been better off to have someone put it together for you.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Archie||||reg||7
Z||000002||Zorba||12-03-2000||01:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> <B>Mario, While we are here.... with all the trouble you've had putting this thing together..... has it occured to you that maybe it would have been cheaper and maybe you would have been better off to have someone put it together for you.<BR>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><B>Thanks.</B> Archie, it may sound like I had a lot of trouble but in sequence:<BR>1. Problem with the wiring. You helped with that.<BR>2. Problem with the starter. Wrong layout. You suggested Powermaster. Worked and works flawlessly. You helped.<P>You see, I used the same manifold on the 305, old engine not knowing that it had a pin hole puncture under the water passage! This caused a huge problem with the other engine. I bought a new engine and failed to notice the manifold body leak until I checked the oil during an idle test in my garage. I just bought a brand new performer rpm which I have looked at carefully. The engine ran fine before, If I haven't screwed it up with the water-oil mix, it should run fine again. To finish the conversion I need to add brake pads, the wheels and decklid.<BR>That's it.<BR>IF I Lived anywhere near you and had the money, I would have you put this together for me. However, locally, NOT A SOUL would want to do this project.  It's been a learning experience for me. Thanks for all your help and prompt response to my emails. <P><B>You're the man.</B><P>||||reg||1
